# VESPER HALL GALLERY -- north wing: portrait gallery (W) and library (E)
# Tileset: TILESET_MUSEUM (Pewter Museum). 15x7 blocks, buffer 273/1300.
# Why a second tileset: the museum's marble checker floor, framed paintings
# (17), the tall framed window (21-22-23), display case (0a-0b-0c), gold
# candelabra statues (24/25), potted palms (20) and free-standing bookcases
# (15) are what make a stately-home gallery; the mansion set has none of them.
# The wings are joined only by a warp (1F door 17 <-> this doormat 03), so
# the tileset switch is invisible to the player.
# Gallery/library divider: wooden rail 01 with a gap at row 3.
# PUZZLE: three portraits (P) of the Vesper line. The diary in the Master
# Suite reads "Dawn, Noon, Dusk -- then the sun goes dark". Examine Dawn
# (east portrait), Noon (centre, left of the window), Dusk (west) in that
# order; the library's corner bookcase (x14,y6) slides aside:
# ship 15 there and `changeblock 28, 12, $05` to reveal the ladder down.
ref PewterMuseum1F
tileset museum
key ,=02 M=03 v=05 w=06 1=01 a=0a b=0b c=0c B=15 P=17 p=20 G=21 H=22 J=23 S=24 t=25
grid:
PwPGHJPw1BBBBBB
,,,,,,,,1,,,,,,
pS,,,,tp1,B,B,,
,,abc,,,,,B,B,,
p,,,,,,p1,,,,,,
,,,,,,,,1,,BB,,
,,,,M,,,1,,,,,v
end
exit DOOR1F 8 13
exit DOOR1F2 9 13
exit LADDER 29 13
obj sign 13 0 PortraitDawn
obj sign 5 0 PortraitNoon
obj sign 1 0 PortraitDusk
obj sign 6 7 CaseEclipseStone
obj trainer 12 9 CollectorPM left 4
obj trainer 22 3 GovernessT down 3
obj trainer 26 9 BurglarFinn left 3
obj item 18 12 TMinLibrary
obj sign 21 6 ShelfNote
